INT. SUBURBAN KITCHEN - NIGHT

Dishes drying on a rack. A school calendar with a circled date. A laptop open on the counter, its screen reflecting off a dark window.

HATTIE BRANDT, 15, in an oversized hoodie, sits cross-legged on a stool, thumbing her phone, a half-eaten bowl of cereal in front of her. She hasn't noticed the milk has gone warm.

The phone vibrates. DAD flashes on the screen. She watches it buzz. Lets it go.

It buzzes again.

She picks up.

HATTIE
What.

ROLAND (V.O.)
(over speaker, a car interior, road noise)
Hattie, hey. I'm outside.

HATTIE
Outside where?

ROLAND (V.O.)
Your house. Out front. In the driveway.

She goes to the window, parts the blinds with two fingers. A car idles at the curb, headlights off, a silhouette behind the wheel.

HATTIE
Mom said you weren't coming till Saturday.

ROLAND (V.O.)
I know what she said.

HATTIE
She's going to freak out.

ROLAND (V.O.)
She's asleep.

HATTIE
She's not asleep. She's pretending to be asleep.

ROLAND (V.O.)
Then she can keep pretending. Come out. Five minutes.

HATTIE
I have school tomorrow.

ROLAND (V.O.)
Then ten minutes. I'll drive you around the block.

Hattie hesitates, hand on the blind. She looks back at the kitchen, the cereal, the calendar. The circled date is tomorrow.

HATTIE
Dad. Why tonight?

ROLAND (V.O.)
Because I've been parked here for an hour trying to knock on the door and I can't.

Silence on the line. Rain starts, soft, on the window.

HATTIE
(quietly)
You can't come in.

ROLAND (V.O.)
I know.

HATTIE
She changed the locks.

ROLAND (V.O.)
I know, sweetheart.

HATTIE
But I can come out.

She takes her hoodie from the chair. Pulls it on over her pajamas, zips it to the chin.

ROLAND (V.O.)
Take an umbrella.

HATTIE
It's drizzling.

ROLAND (V.O.)
Take an umbrella anyway.

She almost laughs. Takes the umbrella from the stand by the door. Pauses at the back stairs, listening to the silence of the house.

HATTIE
Dad?

ROLAND (V.O.)
Yeah.

HATTIE
I'm coming out.

She lowers the phone, still connected, and slips quietly out the door.
